# Generated from .claude/settings.json by `bun scripts/codex-rules.ts`; edit that file, not this one.
# A Codex rule is a word prefix: a Claude rule without a `*` (an exact command) allows arguments after it here.
# Rules whose `*` stands inside a word have no form here; Seismic applies them itself to its Codex workers:
#   Bash(mkdir -p /Users/nick/demos/obeya-*)
#   Bash(mkdir -p /tmp/obeya-*)
#   Bash(bun scripts/scratch-obeya.ts /tmp/obeya-*.json)
#   Bash(bun scripts/scratch-obeya.ts /Users/nick/demos/obeya-*/stage.json)
#   Bash(bun scripts/scratch-obeya.ts /tmp/obeya-*.json --code HEAD)
#   Bash(node /Users/nick/demos/obeya-*/demo.ts)
#   Bash(node /Users/nick/demos/obeya-*/demo.ts --narration)
#   Bash(node /Users/nick/demos/obeya-*/demo.ts --dry)

